1. Identity & Sign-In Investigations
1.1 Successful Sign-In Events (Detailed View)
Purpose
Used to investigate successful sign-ins with full contextual information such as IP, location, user agent, and conditional access state.

Typical use cases

Validate suspicious sign-ins

Review user activity for incident timelines



SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| where ResultType == 0
| where * contains ""
| project TimeGenerated, OriginalRequestId, IPAddress, AppDisplayName, AuthenticationRequirement, ClientAppUsed, ConditionalAccessStatus, UserAgent, Location, LocationDetails

1.2 Sign-In Result Types Overview
Purpose
Provides a high level overview of authentication outcomes for interactive sign-ins.

Typical use cases

Identify spikes in failed sign-ins

Detect authentication issues



SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| where * contains ""
| summarize count() by ResultType
| render barchart

1.3 Sign-In Volume by Application
Purpose
Shows which applications are most frequently used for successful sign-ins.

Typical use cases

Application usage analysis

Identify unexpected app access



SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| where ResultType == 0
| where * contains ""
| summarize count() by AppDisplayName

1.4 Sign-In Activity Over Time (Downtime Detection)
Purpose
Visualizes sign-in volume over time to detect outages, disruptions, or abnormal drops.

Typical use cases

Correlate sign-in failures with change events



SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
| where * contains ""
| summarize SignInCount = count() by bin(TimeGenerated, 30m)
| render timechart with (kind=unstacked)

1.5 Sign-Ins by IP Address and Result Type
Purpose
Highlights authentication behavior per source IP, including success and failure patterns.

Typical use cases

Brute force detection

IP reputation analysis

Incident scoping



SigninLogs
| where * contains ""
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| summarize count() by IPAddress, ResultType
| render barchart
| order by count_ desc

1.6 Sign-Ins by Country and IP
Purpose
Provides geographic insight into successful sign-ins.

Typical use cases

Impossible travel analysis

Geo based threat detection



SigninLogs
| where * contains ""
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| where ResultType == "0"
| summarize count() by Location, IPAddress
| render barchart
| order by count_ desc

1.7 Simplified Sign-In Context View
Purpose
Lightweight version for quick checks without application or CA details.

Typical use cases

Timeline enrichment

User behavior validation



SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| where * contains ""
| where ResultType == "0"
| project TimeGenerated, Location, IPAddress, LocationDetails, ResultType, UserAgent

2. Non-Interactive Sign-Ins
2.1 Service and Background Sign-In Activity
Purpose
Analyzes non-interactive sign-ins such as service principals and background token refreshes.

Typical use cases

Detect abused service accounts

Identify automation anomalies

Investigate token misuse



workspace("prd-glb-mgmt-prod-sntl01-la01").AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(5d)
| where UserPrincipalName contains ""
| summarize count() by Location, bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)
| render timechart

3. Audit Logs & Privileged Access
3.1 General Audit Log Search
Purpose
Generic audit log search across all Azure AD operations.

Typical use cases

Change tracking

Incident scoping

Compliance investigations



AuditLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| where * contains ""

3.2 PIM Invitation Activities
Purpose
Tracks invitation related actions in Privileged Identity Management.

Typical use cases

Review role invitation abuse

Validate onboarding processes

Privileged access audits



AuditLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| where * contains ""
| where OperationName contains "invite"
| extend initiatedByUser = parse_json(InitiatedBy).user.userPrincipalName

3.3 PIM Role Activation Results and Reasons
Purpose
Shows role assignment outcomes including approval result and justification.

Typical use cases

Privileged access reviews

Approval workflow audits

Incident root cause analysis



AuditLogs
| where * contains ""
| where OperationName contains "Add member to role completed"
| extend TargetResourcesParsed = parse_json(TargetResources)
| extend Role = TargetResourcesParsed[0].displayName
| project TimeGenerated, Category, Role, ResultDescription, ResultReason, Result

3.4 Owner or Member Removal Events
Purpose
Tracks removal of owners or members from groups and applications.

Typical use cases

Detect unauthorized privilege removal

Insider threat investigations

Compliance monitoring



AuditLogs
| where * contains ""
| where OperationName contains "Remove member from group" or OperationName contains "Remove owner from application"

4. Infrastructure & Endpoint Security
4.1 New SSH Source IP Detection
Purpose
Identifies public IP addresses successfully authenticating via SSH.

Typical use cases

Detect unauthorized SSH access

Incident validation

Threat hunting on Linux endpoints



Syslog
| where Facility contains "auth" and ProcessName =~ "sshd"
| where SyslogMessage has "Accepted"
| extend SourceIP = extract("(([0-9]{1,3})\\.([0-9]{1,3})\\.([0-9]{1,3})\\.(([0-9]{1,3})))", 1, SyslogMessage)
| where isnotempty(SourceIP)
| where ipv4_is_private(SourceIP) == false
| where HostName contains ""
| summarize count() by SourceIP

5. Log Data Health & Availability
5.1 Table Availability and Data Volume Check
Purpose
Validates which tables contain data and how much, useful for ingestion troubleshooting.

Typical use cases

Verify connector health

Identify missing log sources



union withsource = SrcTable *
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(90d)
| summarize RowCount = count() by TableName = SrcTable
| sort by RowCount desc
